*   **Schedule 2 (Additional Taxes):** Used to report your self-employment tax.
*   **Schedule B (Interest and Ordinary Dividends):** Because your interest income ($2,650) is over the $1,500 threshold, the IRS requires you to fill out Schedule B to list your interest and dividend sources.
